      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Pretty sure the SDK just loops through every camera for the last active one. It should probably grab Camera.main instead or expose a property where users can set their own camera.\nMy freecam script has an option to \"fix\" this issue if interested:\nhttps://github.com/NotAKidOnSteam/FreeCam\n_obvious note: im not associated with vrchat so check the code yourself before trusting, and if you do feel free to PR any changes :)_",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-04-29T17:16:21.642Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "If multiple active Cameras exist in the scene, SDK sometimes uses worng one for grabbing operation on Unity debugging. As a result, you can't grab PhysBones as expected.\n\nWorkaround: Set enabled only on single Camera at initial state. You can enable other Cameras after started.\n\nDemo movie: https://twitter.com/naqtn/status/1520088751078223873\n\nIn this demo, the scene has two Cameras. \"Main Camera\" is targeted to \"Display 1\" and for grabbing test. \"CameraForARenderTexture\" is for a RenderTexture. Both are active. In play mode, you can't grab the bones represented by Cubes. Meanwhile, You can grab them on \"different\" coordinates. If you disable \"CameraForARenderTexture\", then you can grab them on \"proper\" coordinates.\n\nTested with VRCSDK3-AVATAR-2022.04.26.15.46",
  "error": null,
